    "headline": "Jio Platforms IPO set for October 21, targeting $114 billion valuation",
    "essay": "Jio Platforms plans to open its IPO on October 21 and list by October 28 or October 30, aiming to raise about $3.8 billion. The company is targeting a valuation of around $114 billion, or Rs 11 trillion, according to people familiar with the matter. That is below earlier expectations of $130 billion to $170 billion but still makes it India's largest-ever IPO, surpassing Hyundai's Indian unit, which raised $2.9 billion in 2024. The issue is a fresh sale of up to 27 crore new shares, representing about 2.93% of post-issue equity. There is no offer for sale, so proceeds go to Jio Platforms to repay borrowings of Reliance Jio Infocomm and for general corporate purposes. Reliance Industries will remain promoter with a 66.43% pre-issue stake. For Jio Platforms, the listing provides fresh capital and a separate market valuation, which could unlock value for parent RIL by reducing the holding-company discount.",
