    "headline": "Motilal Oswal sees value unlocking and re-rating for RIL from Jio IPO",
    "essay": "Motilal Oswal said the Jio Platforms IPO could unlock value for Reliance Industries and drive a re-rating, as RIL's current price already factors in an 18-36% holding-company discount on its Jio stake. The brokerage values Jio Platforms at Rs 11.2 lakh crore, or about $117 billion, implying 12.1 times FY28 estimated EV/EBITDA. RIL's 66.48% stake is worth about Rs 7.45 lakh crore, or Rs 550 per RIL share, before a 25% discount, giving an attributable value of Rs 413 per share. Motilal Oswal reiterated a Buy rating on RIL with a target price of Rs 1,530. It also expects the IPO and a subsequent tariff hike to support a re-rating for both Jio and Bharti Airtel, and has built in a 15% smartphone tariff hike in December 2026, which could drive 15% EBITDA CAGR over FY26-29. For Jio Platforms, the brokerage's estimates peg FY28 revenue at Rs 1.69 lakh crore and EBITDA at about Rs 95,700 crore, with a 56.6% margin.",
