    },
    {
    "headline": "RIL shareholders may still qualify for Jio IPO quota, but deadline looms",
    "essay": "Reliance Industries shareholders may still have a chance to qualify for the shareholder reservation in the Jio Platforms IPO, but the window is closing. The DRHP defines an eligible RIL shareholder as an individual or HUF holding RIL shares on the date of filing the red herring prospectus (RHP). That date has not been disclosed, so buying RIL shares now could still secure eligibility if the RHP is filed later. The shareholder quota is a separate reserved portion, with a maximum bid of Rs 2 lakh per eligible shareholder. Allotment is proportionate and not guaranteed. Investors can also apply in the retail category. The final reservation size and any discount will be in the RHP. For Jio Platforms, the quota broadens the investor base and could boost demand, but the key date to watch is the RHP filing.",
