      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of Rs 822.3 crore for Q2 FY27, up 12.8% from Rs 729 crore a year earlier. For the first half, billings grew 13.5% to Rs 1,559.3 crore. The recruitment segment, led by Naukri, remained the largest at Rs 613.8 crore, up 12.6% year on year. Management said underlying growth was approximately 14-15% after adjusting for the timing of customer renewals, which can shift billings between quarters.\n\nThe real estate platform 99acres accelerated, with billings up 21.2% to Rs 148.3 crore, faster than the 16.5% growth in Q1. Matchmaking platforms Jeevansathi and Aisle together grew 23.1%, with Jeevansathi billings at Rs 39.7 crore and Aisle up 40%. Adoption of B2B AI products AI-Rex and Talent Pulse increased, with growth in new customer sign-ups and revenue contribution. For the topic, the results show the core recruitment business holding steady, though the stock fell nearly 3% on the day.",
