      "headline": "Shiksha billings fall 27.2% as AI search reduces referrals",
      "essay": "Info Edge's education platform Shiksha saw billings decline 27.2% year on year to Rs 20.5 crore in Q2 FY27, from Rs 28.1 crore. The company attributed the pressure to AI-driven search, which increasingly answers user queries directly and reduces referral traffic to the site. Shiksha is adapting its business model and introducing new offerings to cut its dependence on search, but management expects billings growth to stay under pressure in the interim. For the topic, this highlights a structural challenge from AI search even as other segments grow.",
      "sources": [1, 3, 5]
    }
  ]
