      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of ₹822.3 crore for the September quarter, up 12.8% from ₹729 crore a year earlier. For H1 FY27, billings rose 13.5% to ₹1,559.3 crore from ₹1,373.2 crore. The figures come from a quarterly business update released on 8 October, ahead of the official results, and are still subject to review by the audit committee, board and auditors.\n\nRecruitment Solutions, the segment anchored by Naukri, billed ₹613.8 crore, up 12.6% from ₹545 crore. Management said customer renewals landed differently this quarter and put underlying growth at roughly 14-15%. For H1, recruitment billings were ₹1,166.5 crore, up 14.9%. Underlying recruitment growth was also around 15% in Q1FY27, when reported growth was 17.5%. Adoption of the B2B AI products AI-Rex and Talent Pulse rose, in new sign-ups and revenue.\n\nMatchmaking grew 23.1% overall. Jeevansathi billings rose 18.4% to ₹39.7 crore from ₹33.5 crore, and Aisle rose 40%. H1 Jeevansathi billings were ₹79.3 crore, up 16.3% from ₹68.2 crore. The results rest on recruitment holding its underlying pace, not the headline number.",
