    },
    {
      "headline": "99acres billings accelerate to 21.2% growth in Q2",
      "essay": "99acres was the strongest large segment: billings rose 21.2% to ₹148.3 crore in Q2FY27 from ₹122.4 crore a year earlier. That was quicker than the 16.5% growth in Q1FY27. For the first half, 99acres billings rose 19.2% to ₹258.4 crore.\n\nThe platform kept its share of category traffic, according to SimilarWeb data cited by the company. Web time-share was 49% and app time-share was 59% during July and August 2026. For a business that sells listings to property brokers and developers, holding traffic share while growing billings at a faster rate means the growth is coming from pricing and mix rather than a bigger audience.",
