  "view": "Info Edge billings grew 12.8% in Q2, but that's slower than Q1's 14.4%. Recruitment, the core business, rose 12.6%, while Shiksha fell 27.2%. The Naukri mental health survey is a brand signal, not a financial one. Mixed flow, no clear direction.",
  "stories": [
    {
      "headline": "Info Edge Q2 billings up 12.8%, slower than Q1",
      "essay": "Info Edge reported standalone billings of INR 8.22 billion (USD 63.4 million) for the September quarter, up 12.8% from a year earlier. That pace cooled from the 14.4% annual increase in Q1. Recruitment solutions, the largest segment, grew 12.6% to INR 6.14 billion. Real estate (99acres) rose 21.2% and matrimony (Jeevansathi) rose 18.4%, but education (Shiksha) fell 27.2% to INR 205 million. For the six months ended 30 September, revenue was INR 15.59 billion (USD 161.2 million), up 13.5%. The company noted the update is subject to audit committee, board and auditor review. Shares closed on 8 October at INR 1,182.80, down 3.46%. For the topic, the core recruitment engine is still growing double digits, but the slowdown from Q1 and the Shiksha decline are the details that matter.",
