    {
      "headline": "Naukri survey: 33% fear career loss over mental health talk",
      "essay": "A Naukri survey of nearly 10,000 jobseekers across eight cities and 83 industries found that 61% would openly disclose taking a mental health day. But 33% said losing career opportunities was their biggest concern about discussing mental health at work. Another 32% worried nobody would care, 19% feared being seen as weak, and 16% worried about office gossip. Poor work-life balance was the top workplace factor affecting mental health for 42% of respondents, followed by lack of managerial support at 27% and heavy workloads at 20%. When asked what employers should change, 53% chose clearer boundaries between work and personal time, 22% wanted managers trained to spot burnout, 13% wanted dedicated mental health leave, and 12% wanted better access to counselling. The survey ran ahead of World Mental Health Day on October 10. For Info Edge, this is a brand and engagement signal from its Naukri platform, not a direct revenue driver.",
